# E2E QA Rules (DBO)

Act like a QA engineer: document flows, keep tests isolated, never poison the developer's machine.

**DBO testing policy:** Playwright e2e is the only place for new automated tests. Do not add unit/integration suites under `frontend/` or `backend/` — see `.cursor/rules/go-testing.mdc`.

## Isolation (non-negotiable)

- Run only via `cd e2e && npm test` (or `npm run test:ui`). Never `npx playwright test` alone — `PLAYWRIGHT_API_URL` must come from `run-e2e`.
- Never point tests at a daily backend on `:8080` or the user's Application Support SQLite.
- `/config/reset` is allowed only against the ephemeral API started by the harness.
- Sample PG/MySQL may be shared; always use `uniqueTestSuffix` for object names.

## Spec design

- One user-visible feature/flow per spec file; name it by scenario (`connections.spec.ts`).
- Every meaningful action is a `test.step('…')` — steps are the QA script in the report.
- Prefer independent tests; mega-lifecycles must still clean up on failure.
- Update the feature matrix in `e2e/README.md` when adding/changing coverage.

## Structure

| Layer | Path | Holds |
|-------|------|--------|
| Spec | `tests/*.spec.ts` | Steps + assertions only |
| POM | `pages/` | Locators + UI actions |
| Helpers | `helpers/` | Multi-step flows + `safeCleanup` |
| Fixtures | `fixtures/` | Configs, names, scenario tables |

Do not put long flows in specs or locators in helpers.

## Stability

```ts
// ❌ BAD
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
expect(await el.isVisible()).toBe(true);
await page.locator('.css-abc123').click();

// ✅ GOOD
await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Yes' })).toBeVisible();
await page.getByTestId('add-connection').click();
```

- Prefer `getByRole` / `getByLabel` / `getByTestId`; avoid CSS/XPath unless no contract exists.
- Use web-first `await expect(…).toBeVisible()` — never bare `isVisible()` checks.
- Ban new fixed sleeps; wait on UI/network assertions.
- Always wrap connection-creating tests with `withConnectionCleanup` (or equivalent `try/finally`).
- Never “fix” flakes with retries/`waitForTimeout`; fix selectors, isolation, or product testids.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Affected `e2e/tests/<file>.spec.ts` passes via `npm test -- tests/<file>.spec.ts`
- [ ] Feature matrix row updated if coverage changed
- [ ] No secrets committed; `.env` stays local
- [ ] For harness-only checks, prefer `harness-smoke.spec.ts` (no sample DB)
